        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "bfad9ecb-9755-5610-aebb-829cab219bac",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Maurice Level, Alice Hoffman\n- Places: Paris, Pigalle\n- Organizations: le Théâtre du Grand-Guignol\n- Works: Practical Magic\n- Topics: fiction, drama, macabre short stories, young-adult literature, children's literature\n\nFacts:\n- Maurice Level was born on August 29, 1875, and was a French writer of fiction and drama.\n- Maurice Level specialized in macabre short stories that were regularly printed in Paris newspapers.\n- Some of Maurice Level's stories were staged by le Théâtre du Grand-Guignol, a repertory company in Paris's Pigalle district devoted to melodramatic productions emphasizing blood and gore.\n- Alice Hoffman was born on March 16, 1952, and is an American novelist and writer of young-adult and children's literature.\n- Alice Hoffman is best known for her 1995 novel Practical Magic.\n- Practical Magic was adapted into a film of the same name in 1998.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
