        "text": "Page: Maurice Level. Sentence: Maurice Level (August 29, 1875 – April 15, 1926) was a French writer of fiction and drama who specialized in short stories of the macabre which were printed regularly in the columns of Paris newspapers and sometimes staged by \"le Théâtre du Grand-Guignol\", the repertory company in Paris's Pigalle district devoted to melodramatic productions which emphasized blood and gore.\nPage: Alice Hoffman. Sentence: Alice Hoffman (born March 16, 1952) is an American novelist and young-adult and children's writer, best known for her 1995 novel \"Practical Magic\", which was adapted for a 1998 film of the same name.",
